<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN">
<html>
<head>
  <meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1"
 http-equiv="content-type">
  <title>Sufaces using jmol</title>
  <meta content="J. Gutow" name="author">
  <meta content="Orbital display using jmol" name="description">
  <meta
 content="Page design and layout by J. Gutow 5-2006, page written by perl script orbtohtml.pl"
 name="details">
  <meta
 content="This page is designed to have the text and normal html edited in a standard web design"
 name="instr1">
  <meta
 content="program.  The javascript is to control the jmol applet (see below).  It is best to use"
 name="instr2">
  <meta
 content="the perl scripts to generate the proper java script to allow orbital display.  It is"
 name="instr3">
  <meta
 content="important to have all the gzipped files in the same directory as the .html file.  The"
 name="instr4">
  <meta
 content="files needed are: 1) a gzipped file with the atom coordinates, in any of the formats Jmol"
 name="instr5">
  <meta
 content="can read. 2) a gzipped gaussian cube file for each of the orbitals to be displayed.  To"
 name="instr6">
  <meta
 content="save loading time it seems to be better to avoid including the atom coordinates in the"
 name="instr7">
  <meta
 content="cube files.  It is also recommended that the file names for the surfaces correspond to"
 name="instr8">
  <meta
 content="reasonable names for the orbitals as the file names are used to generate the menu items"
 name="instr9">
  <meta content="that appear in the popup menus for selecting orbitals."
 name="instr10">
  <meta
 content="The relative path to Jmol on your server must be correct below!!"
 name="instr11">
  <script src="../../Applets/Java/Jmol/Jmol.js"></script>
</head>
<body style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(153, 255, 255);"
 alink="#000099" link="#000099" vlink="#990099">
<div style="text-align: center;"><big><big><span
 style="font-weight: bold;">Atomic Orbital Viewer<br>
</span></big></big>
<div style="text-align: left;"><big><big><span
 style="font-weight: bold;"></span></big></big>&nbsp;&nbsp; On
the left in the table below is a window with a green dot in it.&nbsp;
The green
dot represents the location of a chlorine nucleus (significantly
enlarged so that you can see it). On the right hand side are four
pull-down menus from which you can choose an orbital to display.&nbsp;
The electronic configuration of a ground state
chlorine is [Ne]3s<sup>2</sup>3p<sup>5</sup> (1s<sup>2</sup>2s<sup>2</sup>2p<sup>6</sup>3s<sup>2</sup>3p<sup>5</sup>).&nbsp;
This means that the 4s, 3d and 4p orbitals shown are unoccupied;&nbsp;
thus their extent and energy are somewhat different than would be found
for orbitals with electrons in them.&nbsp; The orbitals appear in
the pull-down menus from lowest (at top) to highest (at bottom) energy.
<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp; These orbital images are based on calculations done
using
the <a href="http://www.msg.ameslab.gov/GAMESS/GAMESS.html">GAMESS</a><sup>1</sup>
<span style="font-style: italic;">ab initio</span> quantum mechanics
package and <a href="http://www.scl.ameslab.gov/%7Ebrett/MacMolPlt/">MacMolPlt
5.6</a>.<sup>2</sup> These orbitals are generated from the GAMESS
.log
file of a single point energy calculation on a ground state Cl at the
6-311G++(2d,p)
level of theory.<br>
<br>
<span style="font-style: italic;">Some recommendations on using the
viewer:</span> 1) By default the orbital surfaces are displayed
as solid. When looking at more than one orbital simultaneously it
is usually better to switch to the mesh display so that you can see
through the intersecting surfaces. 2) Zoom in and out.&nbsp;
These orbitals vary greatly in size.<br>
<br>
<span style="font-style: italic;">Other web sites with nice orbital
pictures:</span> Mark Winter's <a
 href="http://www.shef.ac.uk/chemistry/orbitron/">Orbitron
site</a> from Sheffield University in England has very pretty pictures.<br>
<br>
<big><big><span style="font-weight: bold;"></span></big></big>
<table style="width: 100%; text-align: left;" border="1" cellpadding="2"
 cellspacing="2">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td style="vertical-align: top;">
      <script>
jmolInitialize("../../Applets/Java/Jmol");
jmolApplet(300, "load Cl_6-311++(2p,d).log.gz; spacefill 2%; background white"); 
jmolBr();
jmolHtml("This image may be rotated and zoomed.  See below for more instructions.");
        </script>
      <br>
      </td>
      <td style="vertical-align: top;">
      <div style="text-align: right;"> </div>
      <form>
        <div style="text-align: right;"> </div>
        <table style="width: 100%; text-align: left;" border="0"
 cellpadding="2" cellspacing="2">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td colspan="1" rowspan="1"
 style="vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;"><span
 style="font-weight: bold;">Orbital
1:</span><br>
              </td>
              <td style="vertical-align: top;">
              <script>
		jmolMenu([
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete;','none'],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl1s.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl1s.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl1s"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl2s.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl2s.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl2s"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl2px.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl2px.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl2px"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl2py.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl2py.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl2py"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl2pz.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl2pz.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl2pz"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3s.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3s.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3s"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3px.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3px.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3px"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3py.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3py.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3py"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3pz.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3pz.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3pz"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl4s.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl4s.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl4s"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3dxy.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3dxy.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3dxy"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3d_z^2.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3d_z^2.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3d_z^2"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3dx^2-y^2.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3dx^2-y^2.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3dx^2-y^2"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3dxz.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3dxz.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3dxz"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl3dyz.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl3dyz.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl3dyz"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl4px.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl4px.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl4px"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl4py.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl4py.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl4py"],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 "Cl4pz.cube.gz"; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 "Cl4pz.cube.gz";color isosurface blue;',"Cl4pz"],
		]);
		</script>
