      <td colspan="2" rowspan="1" style="vertical-align: top;">
      <div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Instructions
for using Jmol to display
orbitals</span>: <br>
      </div>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose which orbitals to display by selecting them the
orbital popup menus. You can control orbital color and fill mode
by selecting the appropriate options following each orbital menu.&nbsp;
        </li>
        <li>ROTATE the image by
holding
down the mouse button while moving the cursor over the image. </li>
        <li>ZOOM by holding down the shift key while moving the cursor
up
(decrease magnification) or down (increase magnification) on top of the
image. </li>
        <li>Other options available in the control menu accessible by
holding
the mouse button down while the cursor is over "Jmol" in the lower
right corner (right click also works on a multibutton mouse). </li>
        <li>For more info about Jmol go to <a target="_blank"
 href="http://www.jmol.org">www.jmol.org.</a></li>
      </ol>
